course: dictionary
lesson: 14257
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Look at the words around them to find out which meaning the writer wants. «The vet said Biscuit, our cat, was neutered this morning.» Here neutered is about an animal, so it means the cat had a small operation so that it cannot have babies.
explain: The second meaning is more formal. «The judges neutered the new law, so it could no longer protect anyone.» Nobody can have an operation on a law. Neutered means made weaker or less effective, and the clues are law and could no longer protect.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably got it right. People also use other words for a neutered pet, such as spayed and fixed.
fact: «Neutered» means that a pet, like a cat or dog, has had a small operation by a vet so that it cannot have babies.
fact: «Neutered» can also mean made weaker or less effective, as in «a neutered law».
fact: «Spayed» is the polite word for a female animal that has been neutered.
fact: «Fixed» and «done» are informal words for neutered, used mostly in the US, Canada and Australia.
fact: Owners often get pets neutered to stop unwanted kittens and puppies from being born.
exercise: «The vet said Biscuit, our cat, was neutered this morning.» What does neutered mean here? | Was very hungry | *Had a small operation so that it cannot have babies | Was taken for a long walk | Was given a brand new name
exercise: «The judges neutered the new law, so it could no longer protect anyone.» What does neutered mean here? | Put inside a box | Made bigger and stronger | Painted bright blue | *Made weaker and less effective
exercise: Which word is the polite word for a female animal that has been neutered? | Hungry | Lost | *Spayed | Soaking wet
test: «We got our puppy neutered so he would not have puppies.» What does neutered mean here? | Trained to sit and stay | *Had a small operation so that he cannot have babies | Fed a special diet | Sent to live on a farm
test: In the US, a friend says, «We got our cat fixed.» What does fixed mean? | Repaired, like a broken toy | Painted a new colour | *Neutered, so the cat cannot have babies | Tied up outside
exam: Which sentence uses neutered with its second meaning, made weaker? | «Our neutered dog is calm and sleepy.» | «The vet neutered the young male kitten this morning.» | «We need to get our rabbit neutered soon.» | *«The minister's plan was neutered by the new rules, leaving almost nothing.»
